 **[Cache expensive Mathematical Look-Up Tables]**
 **Learning:** When processing 8-bit color channels, precomputing a 256-element Look-Up Table (LUT) array (e.g., `[u32; 256]`) directly inside the function effectively eliminates expensive floating-point operations (like division and `f32::round()`) from the hot per-pixel loop without the overhead of thread-local storage.
-**Action:** Use fixed-size stack arrays (`[u32; 256]`) for per-channel LUTs when appropriate to bypass floating-point math in tight per-pixel loops.
